course: dictionary
lesson: 8443
title: Adverbs: the word safely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Safely is an adverb. An adverb tells us how, when or where something happens. Safely tells us how: «Cross the road safely» means the way you cross, so you cross without danger.
explain: Safely has two meanings. The first is without danger, harm or accident: «In 1970 an oxygen tank exploded on Apollo 13, and the crew worked out how to bring them home safely.» The second is with no risk of being wrong: «You can safely say it was fun.»
explain: Use the words around it to check which meaning fits. In «a line painted on its side shows how deep it may safely sit», safely means without danger, because the line keeps the ship from sinking too low. Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Safely is an adverb. It tells how something is done, like «ride a bike safely».
fact: Safely means without danger, harm or accident.
fact: Safely can also mean with no risk of being wrong, as in «You can safely say it was fun».
fact: Safe is the adjective, and safely is its adverb form. The forms are safely, more safely and most safely.
fact: Useful phrases include «get home safely», «drive safely», «safely back» and «arrived safely».
exercise: Kai rides his bike safely to school. What does safely tell us? | Who he rides with | *How he rides | Where he rides | When he rides
exercise: «The crew could come home safely.» What does safely mean here? | Very loudly | *Without danger or harm | Very quickly | Very angrily
exercise: «Store the food safely so the bears stay away.» Which word is the adverb? | campsite | *safely | bears | food
test: Which phrase means arrived without being hurt? | arrived angrily | arrived late | *arrived safely | arrived loudly
test: «You can safely say it was fun.» What does safely mean here? | Without any noise | Very slowly | With great care for the table | *With no risk of being wrong
exam: Which sentence uses safely to mean without danger? | *Please get home safely tonight | It was a bright and sunny day | The cat slept on the warm mat | Tom ran very fast to the shop
